    <!--
        There are no suppressions right now, and that is the point: both that used to live
        here were Marten advisories, and step 30 removed them by fixing the cause.

        GHSA-vmw2-qwm8-x84c (SQL injection via the full-text `regConfig` parameter, fixed
        in Marten 8.37.0) and GHSA-rfx3-98h7-v3xp (SQL injection via unescaped string
        literals in the LINQ provider and tenant management, fixed in Marten 9.13.0) were
        both suppressed while 03-retarget-net10.md deliberately held Marten at 7.31.1. Each
        carried an argument that it was not exploitable here, and each said "Remove this
        suppression when Marten is upgraded." Marten is now 9.45.0, past both fixes, so the
        arguments are no longer load-bearing and the audit is free to fail on them again.
    -->

</Project>
